{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374798492,"sessionID":"ses_f9c8e48c5ffeFcOrr6Qvqf72Tj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6726bf1e6f3947dfaa3376d6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n2: \n3: Kernel design (grid-stride variant):\n4:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n5:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n6:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n7:     spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n8:     store.\n9:   - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n10:     param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n11:       * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n12:             y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n13:       * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n14:             y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n15:   - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n16:     on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n17:   - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n18:     1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n19:   - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n20:     values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n21:     identical-form evaluation.\n22: \"\"\"\n23: \n24: import math\n25: \n26: import torch\n27: \n28: import asc\n29: import asc2\n30: \n31: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n32: \n33: _C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n34: _C0_TANH = 2.0 * math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n35: _K_TANH = 0.044715\n36: \n37: _ERF_TILE = 512\n38: _TANH_TILE = 1024\n39: _MAX_CORES = 72\n40: \n41: \n42: @asc2.jit\n43: def _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n44:                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n45:                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n46:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n47:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n48:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n49:                         unroll_factor=2):\n50:         off = t * tile_size\n51:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n52:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n53:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n54:         z = asc2.abs(xf) * _C1_ERF\n55:         t = 1.0 / (1.0 + 0.5 * z)\n56:         p = t * 0.17087277 - 0.82215223\n57:         p = p * t + 1.48851587\n58:         p = p * t - 1.13520398\n59:         p = p * t + 0.27886807\n60:         p = p * t - 0.18628806\n61:         p = p * t + 0.09678418\n62:         p = p * t + 0.37409196\n63:         p = p * t + 1.00002368\n64:         p = p * t - 1.26551223\n65:         efc = t * asc2.exp(p - z * z)\n66:         hxh = xf * 0.5 * efc\n67:         neg = xf - hxh\n68:         yf = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, neg, hxh)\n69:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n70: \n71: \n72: @asc2.jit\n73: def _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n74:                       size: int, num_tiles: int,\n75:                       tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n76:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n77:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n78:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n79:                         unroll_factor=2):\n80:         off = t * tile_size\n81:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n82:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n83:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n84:         x2 = xf * xf\n85:         x3 = x2 * xf\n86:         s = (xf + x3 * _K_TANH) * _C0_TANH\n87:         em = asc2.exp(asc2.minimum(s, 0.0))\n88:         ea = asc2.exp(-asc2.abs(s))\n89:         yf = xf * em / (1.0 + ea)\n90:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n91: \n92: \n93: def gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n94:     \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n95:     ensure_npu_platform()\n96:     assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n97:         f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n98:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n99:         x = x.contiguous()\n100:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n101:     size = x.numel()\n102:     if size == 0:\n103:         return out\n104:     if approximate == \"none\":\n105:         tile = _ERF_TILE\n106:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n107:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n108:         _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n109:     else:\n110:         tile = _TANH_TILE\n111:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n112:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n113:         _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n114:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 114 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n    identical-form evaluation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n_C0_TANH = 2.0 * math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n_K_TANH = 0.044715\n\n_ERF_TILE = 512\n_TANH_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                     tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        z = asc2.abs(xf) * _C1_ERF\n        t = 1.0 / (1.0 + 0.5 * z)\n        p = t * 0.17087277 - 0.82215223\n        p = p * t + 1.48851587\n        p = p * t - 1.13520398\n        p = p * t + 0.27886807\n        p = p * t - 0.18628806\n        p = p * t + 0.09678418\n        p = p * t + 0.37409196\n        p = p * t + 1.00002368\n        p = p * t - 1.26551223\n        efc = t * asc2.exp(p - z * z)\n        hxh = xf * 0.5 * efc\n        neg = xf - hxh\n        yf = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, neg, hxh)\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        x2 = xf * xf\n        x3 = x2 * xf\n        s = (xf + x3 * _K_TANH) * _C0_TANH\n        em = asc2.exp(asc2.minimum(s, 0.0))\n        ea = asc2.exp(-asc2.abs(s))\n        yf = xf * em / (1.0 + ea)\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n        f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if approximate == \"none\":\n        tile = _ERF_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    else:\n        tile = _TANH_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":114,"totalLines":114,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788374798481,"end":1788374798490}},"id":"prt_06371ce84001D8r7k86VOF7BNR","sessionID":"ses_f9c8e48c5ffeFcOrr6Qvqf72Tj","messageID":"msg_06371c74a001DDCPpd4RVf8Zip"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374799098,"sessionID":"ses_f9c8e48c5ffeFcOrr6Qvqf72Tj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ab085a6752544919b1e4900c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n2: \n3: Repair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\n4: must remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n5: `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n6: \n7: The candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n8: `job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n9: \n10: - case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n11: - case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n12: - case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n13: - case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n14: \n15: BF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n16: `1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n17: `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\n18: copy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\n19: all dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\n20: only `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n21: \n22: The first repair attempt is rejected. It substituted a different\n23: Abramowitz-Stegun-style polynomial, evaluated it at `abs(x)` instead of\n24: `abs(x)/sqrt(2)`, and did not implement the required Numerical Recipes Horner\n25: chain. Replace that rejected exact-mode body using the now-explicit coefficient\n26: sequence in the skill reference; do not merely review it for syntax.\n27: \n28: The second repair attempt implemented the required formula, but the exact-v2\n29: compile gate rejected every exact-mode specialization. With\n30: `tile_size=2048`, `unroll_factor=2`, reported UB use is 819968 bytes for\n31: FP16/BF16 and 795392 bytes for FP32, above the 253952-byte limit. The three\n32: tanh specializations pass at tile 1024 and use 172032--184320 bytes. Apply the\n33: updated measured tile rule from the skill reference: exact mode must use the\n34: safe 512-element tile with unroll factor 2. Keep the stable formulas and do not\n35: regress the already-passing tanh branch.\n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","text":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n\nThe first repair attempt is rejected. It substituted a different\nAbramowitz-Stegun-style polynomial, evaluated it at `abs(x)` instead of\n`abs(x)/sqrt(2)`, and did not implement the required Numerical Recipes Horner\nchain. Replace that rejected exact-mode body using the now-explicit coefficient\nsequence in the skill reference; do not merely review it for syntax.\n\nThe second repair attempt implemented the required formula, but the exact-v2\ncompile gate rejected every exact-mode specialization. With\n`tile_size=2048`, `unroll_factor=2`, reported UB use is 819968 bytes for\nFP16/BF16 and 795392 bytes for FP32, above the 253952-byte limit. The three\ntanh specializations pass at tile 1024 and use 172032--184320 bytes. Apply the\nupdated measured tile rule from the skill reference: exact mode must use the\nsafe 512-element tile with unroll factor 2. Keep the stable formulas and do not\nregress the already-passing tanh branch.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":35,"totalLines":35,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","time":{"start":1788374799085,"end":1788374799097}},"id":"prt_06371d0ef001wvW7RqmDjjSPyg","sessionID":"ses_f9c8e48c5ffeFcOrr6Qvqf72Tj","messageID":"msg_06371c74a001DDCPpd4RVf8Zip"}}
